@startuml M6-Search-Example

' Concrete example: user searches for "python" (11 numbered steps)
' Shows complete query flow with actual data and real TF-IDF scores
' Step 1-2: Parse and normalize query
' Step 3-4: Look up term in distributed index (returns 3 candidate documents)
' Step 5-6: Calculate TF-IDF scores (0.85, 0.62, 0.45)
' Step 7-8: Apply metadata boosts (stars, language, topics)
' Step 9-10: Combine scores (75% TF-IDF + 25% metadata)
' Step 11: Rank results and format for display

!define BGCOLOR #F5F5F5
skinparam backgroundColor BGCOLOR
skinparam sequenceActorBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam sequenceActorBorderColor #333
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #E8F4F8
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #1F77B4
skinparam arrowColor #333
skinparam shadowing false

title M6 Search Engine - Complete Query Example: "python"

actor User
participant CLI
participant "Query\nParser"
participant "Query\nProcessor"
participant "Search\nService"
participant "M4 Store"
participant "TF-IDF\nScorer"
participant "Metadata\nBoost"
participant "Score\nCalculator"
participant "Results\nRanker"
participant "Result\nFormatter"

autonumber

User -> CLI: search python

CLI -> "Query\nParser": input: "python"

"Query\nParser" -> "Query\nParser": parse query\noutput: {term: "python"}

"Query\nParser" -> "Query\nProcessor": {term: "python"}

"Query\nProcessor" -> "Query\nProcessor": normalize text:\n"python" -> lowercase -> stem

"Query\nProcessor" -> "Search\nService": processed: "python"

"Search\nService" -> "M4 Store": lookup index:\nwhere term = "python"?

"M4 Store" -> "M4 Store": find in\ndistributed store\n(Node 2)

"M4 Store" -> "Search\nService": return postings:\nterm: "python"\npostings: [123, 456, 789]\ndf: 3

"Search\nService" -> "TF-IDF\nScorer": documents: [123, 456, 789]\nquery term: "python"

"TF-IDF\nScorer" -> "TF-IDF\nScorer": calculate TF-IDF:\ndoc 123: 0.85\ndoc 456: 0.62\ndoc 789: 0.45

"TF-IDF\nScorer" -> "Metadata\nBoost": TF-IDF scores

"Metadata\nBoost" -> "Metadata\nBoost": apply boosts:\ndoc 123: +0.1 (stars)\ndoc 456: +0.05 (lang)\ndoc 789: +0.0

"Metadata\nBoost" -> "Score\nCalculator": TF-IDF + boosts

"Score\nCalculator" -> "Score\nCalculator": combine scores:\nTF-IDF weight: 75%\nMetadata weight: 25%\n\ndoc 123: 0.85*0.75+0.1*0.25=0.663\ndoc 456: 0.62*0.75+0.05*0.25=0.478\ndoc 789: 0.45*0.75+0.0*0.25=0.338

"Score\nCalculator" -> "Results\nRanker": scored documents

"Results\nRanker" -> "Results\nRanker": sort by score:\n[123:0.663, 456:0.478, 789:0.338]

"Results\nRanker" -> "Result\nFormatter": ranked results

"Result\nFormatter" -> "Result\nFormatter": format output:\n1. python-awesome\n   (123 stars, Python)\n2. python-basics\n   (45 stars, Python)\n3. python-data\n   (12 stars, Python)

"Result\nFormatter" -> CLI: formatted results

CLI -> User: display:\n1. python-awesome (123 stars)\n2. python-basics (45 stars)\n3. python-data (12 stars)

note right of "Query\nParser"
Step 2-3: Parse and normalize
query string to standardized form
end note

note right of "Search\nService"
Step 4-5: Lookup index in
distributed M4 store
end note

note right of "Score\nCalculator"
Step 8: Final scoring combines
TF-IDF (75%) + metadata (25%)
end note

note right of "Result\nFormatter"
Step 10: Format results with
metadata (stars, language)
end note

@enduml
